[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  ⚡  Ubuntu → ZFS\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;36m[1. Scan disk + choose method]\u001b[0m | 2. Prepare disk | 3. Convert ext4 to ZFS | 4. Finish disk + boot setup\r\n  5. Snapshots + recovery + growth\r\n\r\n  Scan the selected data disk and its mount settings\r\n\r\n\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  ⚡  Ubuntu → ZFS\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;36m[1. Scan disk + choose method]\u001b[0m | 2. Prepare disk | 3. Convert ext4 to ZFS | 4. Finish disk + boot setup\r\n  5. Snapshots + recovery + growth\r\n\r\nSelect a conversion method\r\n\r\nMake a full offsite backup before proceeding. Conversion can destroy data.\r\n\r\nMigration options for /dev/vdc (1.07/4.14 GB used):\r\n  1) 50/50: keep ext4 until the ZFS copy is verified\r\n\r\n  2) Slice-by-slice: recycle verified ext4 blocks (experimental) — unavailable for data volumes\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m  3) External backup: verify an independent archive, then restore ◀ SELECTED\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  4) ERASE: discard data; root gets limited settings restoration\r\n\r\n  q) Cancel\r\nExternal backup needs a destination you explicitly select. Review the plan before conversion.\r\nNAME   PATH      SIZE FSTYPE MOUNTPOINTS\r\nvdc    /dev/vdc    4G        \r\n`-vdc1 /dev/vdc1   4G ext4   /mnt/data\r\nbackup data volume: /dev/vdc1 on /dev/vdc; final pool zfsify_4ffbe5d4061a4490 at /mnt/data\r\n[ ext4 ] -> [ verified archive on separate Volume / remote ] -> [ full ZFS ] -> [ restored data ]\r\nWork logs: /var/lib/zfsify-volume.VPssbelC; stop applications using /mnt/data before proceeding.\r\nExplicit non-interactive consent: proceeding with the selected plan.\r\n\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  ⚡  Ubuntu → ZFS\u001b[0m\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[K\r\n\r  ✓ 1. Scan disk + choose method | \u001b[1;36m[2. Prepare disk]\u001b[0m | 3. Convert ext4 to ZFS | 4. Finish disk + boot setup\u001b[K\r\n\r  5. Snapshots + recovery + growth\u001b[K\r\n\r\u001b[K\r\n\r  · RUNNING  ·  STEP: Update Ubuntu package indexes